-- #1351. `fmodI.mth` is a standalone (required: methodDispatchIdxRef's only reader is
-- gated on standaloneValuesRef, so without a standalone shadow the table is never
-- read at all -- see claim.txt's trap note). `amodI.IA.mth : a -> Int -> Int` puts the
-- typaram at dispatch index 0; `zmodI.IZ.mth : Int -> b -> Int` puts it at index 1, and
-- IZ carries the program's only impl. Importing fmodI before amodI before zmodI:
--
-- ⚠️ The third clause names `IZ` deliberately -- see claim.txt's RE-POINTED note. Without
-- it, #1354 unit A's S1 interface-operand scoping means neither interface is nameable
-- here, `mth` is not a shadow, and the bare-name dispatch-index table is never reached,
-- so the graph stops exercising this defect. Naming either interface restores it.
import fmodI.{mth}
import amodI.{af}
import zmodI.{IZ, zf}

main = println (mth "abc" 5 + af 0 + zf 0)
